# Woodland Weavemaster, a 1/2 with vigilance: "Whenever another Elf you control enters, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.
# {T}: Add X mana of any one color, where X is this creature's power. Spend this mana only to cast Elf spells and activate abilities of
# Elf sources." On turn 3 Bot1 casts a Llanowar Elves, which makes the Weavemaster a 2/3 (Bot2's Elf would not), then taps it for two
# mana of one color, {G}{G}, that pay only for Elf things: not a Grizzly Bears, nor the Mountaincycling of an Oliphaunt (not an Elf
# source), but the Forestcycling of a Wirewood Guardian, an Elf card in the hand (CR 106.6). On turn 4 the Weavemaster is a 1/2 again
# (until end of turn) and on turn 5 a tap gives a single mana, {G}, for its power of 1 (X is its power as it is activated), which pays for an Elvish Mystic, an Elf spell (CR 106.6): the Weavemaster is a 2/3 again.

